## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical design of data contracts, lineage, and governance in a multi-domain Azure data mesh, with real ingestion patterns.

## Key Concepts
- Data contracts across domains
- End-to-end lineage with Purview
- Delta Lake schema evolution and time travel
- Domain isolation via access controls
- Canary tests for contract changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// pseudo contract test for incoming record
function validateContract(record, contract) {
  // contract = {schema: {...}, required: [...], checks: [...]}
  if (!contract.required.every(k => k in record)) return false;
  // simple type checks
  for (let key of Object.keys(contract.schema)) {
    if (typeof record[key] !== contract.schema[key]) return false;
  }
  // custom checks
  return contract.checks.every(fn => fn(record));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you version contracts and rollback a breaking change?
- How would you monitor contract violations and auto-generate lineage dashboards?

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates the ability to design a comprehensive lakehouse architecture that seamlessly integrates streaming and batch data ingestion while maintaining data quality, governance, and disaster recovery capabilities within the Azure ecosystem.

## Key Concepts

- Delta Live Tables for automated ETL with incremental processing
- Schema drift management through auto-evolution capabilities
- Structured streaming integration from Azure Event Hubs
- Batch data ingestion from SFTP sources
- Data quality enforcement using Delta Live Tables Expectations
- PII protection through custom UDFs and governance controls
- End-to-end lineage tracking with Azure Purview integration
- Cross-region disaster recovery using ADLS Gen2 geo-replication
- Backfill strategies with dedicated pipeline runs

## Code Example

```javascript
// PII masking implementation
function maskPII(record) {
  const r = {...record};
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/(.{2}).*(@.*)/, '$1***$2');
  if (r.phone) r.phone = r.phone.replace(/(\d{3})\d{4}(\d{4})/, '$1****$2');
  return r;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This probes practical data governance, real-time-to-batch pipelines, and DR considerations in Azure for large-scale workloads.

## Key Concepts
- Event Hubs ingestion and Spark Structured Streaming
- Delta Lake with schema drift handling
- PII masking at ingestion
- Purview lineage and data residency compliance
- Cross-region DR and serverless analytics

## Code Example
```javascript
// PII masking pseudo-code
function maskPII(record) {
  if (!record?.email) return record;
  record.email = record.email.replace(/[^@]+@/, '*****@');
  return record;
}
```

